{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "EXO",
  "chapter": 2,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And there went a man of the house of Levi, and married a daughter of Levi.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the woman conceived, and bore a son: and when she saw him that he ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was a",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " goodly ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "child",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", she hid him three months.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when she could no longer hide him, she took for him an ark of bulrushes, and daubed it with slime and with pitch, and put the child therein; and she laid ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the flags by the river's brink.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And his sister stood afar off, to know what would be done to him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the daughter of Pharaoh came down to wash ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "herself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " at the river, and her maidens walked along by the river's side: and when she saw the ark among the flags, she sent her maid to fetch it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when she had opened ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", she saw the child: and behold, the babe wept. And she had compassion on him, and said, This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the Hebrews' children.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said his sister to Pharaoh's daughter, Shall I go, and call to thee a nurse of the Hebrew women, that she may nurse the child for thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Pharaoh's daughter said to her, Go. And the maid went and called the child's mother.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Pharaoh's daughter said to her, Take this child away and nurse it for me, and I will give ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy wages. And the woman took the child and nursed it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the child grew, and she brought him to Pharaoh's daughter, and he became her son. And she called his name Moses: and she said, Because I drew him out of the water.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass in those days, when Moses was grown, that he went out to his brethren, and looked on their burdens: and he spied an Egyptian smiting a Hebrew, one of his brethren.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he looked this way and that way, and when he saw that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no man, he slew the Egyptian, and hid him in the sand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he went out the second day, behold, two men of the Hebrews strove together: and he said to him that did the wrong, Why smitest thou thy fellow?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said, Who made thee a prince and a judge over us? intendest thou to kill me, as thou killedst the Egyptian? And Moses feared, and said, Surely this thing is known.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now when Pharaoh heard this thing, he sought to slay Moses. But Moses fled from the face of Pharaoh, and dwelt in the land of Midian: and he sat down by a well.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now the priest of Midian had seven daughters: and they came and drew ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "water",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and filled the troughs to water their father's flock.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the shepherds came and drove them away: but Moses stood up and helped them, and watered their flock.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when they came to Reuel their father, he said, How ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is it that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " you are come so soon to day?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they said, An Egyptian delivered us from the hand of the shepherds, and also drew ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "water",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " enough for us, and watered the flock.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said to his daughters, And where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he? why ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ye have left the man? call him, that he may eat bread.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Moses was content to dwell with the man: and he gave Moses Zipporah his daughter.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And she bore ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a son, and he called his name Gershom: for he said, I have been a stranger in a strange land.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass in process of time, that the king of Egypt died: and the children of Israel sighed by reason of the bondage, and they cried; and their cry ascended to God, by reason of the bondage.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And God heard their groaning, and God remembered his covenant with Abraham, with Isaac, and with Jacob.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.2.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.2.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And God looked upon the children of Israel, and God had respect to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
